[TITLE]
WaterFiberSim - single pipe: 1 km PE100 SDR11 DN110 (P1), downhill 2 % (20 m -> 0 m), reservoir at the top, all the demand at the far end (N1).
Same total demand as the street S1 (11 x 0.3 = 3.3 L/s, pattern DAILY) but taken in one place: the whole flow
runs along the whole pipe. N0 is only the joint with the feeder P0 (10 m) from the reservoir: no demand.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev_m   Demand_LPS   Pattern
 N0   20       0
 N1   0        3.3          DAILY

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head_m
 R1   70

[TANKS]

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1  Node2  Length_m     Diameter_mm  Roughness_HW  MinorLoss      Status
; feeder (no fibre). Pipe: PE100 SDR11 OD 110 -> ID 90, C 140 (EPANET Table 3.2, plastic)
 P0   R1     N0     10           90           140           0              Open
 P1   N0     N1     1000         90           140           0              Open

[PUMPS]

[VALVES]

[PATTERNS]
;ID      Hourly multipliers (00-23), mean 1
 DAILY  0.50 0.40 0.35 0.35 0.40 0.60
 DAILY  0.90 1.40 1.60 1.40 1.20 1.20
 DAILY  1.30 1.20 1.00 0.90 0.90 1.10
 DAILY  1.40 1.60 1.50 1.20 0.90 0.65

[TIMES]
 Duration           24:00
 Hydraulic Timestep 1:00
 Pattern Timestep   1:00
 Report Timestep    1:00
 Start ClockTime    0:00

[OPTIONS]
 Units              LPS
 Headloss           H-W
 Pattern            1

[COORDINATES]
;Node  X    Y
 R1    -50   0
 N0    0     0
 N1    1000  0

[END]
